  data: {
    LLM: "Pure Chance. RÄƒzboi is a game of zero-volition; the deck order is fixed once dealt. However, in physical play, the way you place won cards at the bottom of your deck matters. Grouping face-cards together can lead to 'Streaks' that allow you to win several rounds in a row.\n\nThe 'End-Game' Shuffle: Physical cards often get 'clumped' after a large war. Since wars are often decided by face-cards, if you win a 20-card war, be careful how you order the won cards. Putting your high cards at the very bottom might mean you are vulnerable to a 'War' later when your stack is low.\n\nStamina Management: The game can last a very long time. In competitive settings, 'Card-Tracking' isn't necessary, but mental focus is. If you lose several wars, stay calmâ€”the deck order will cycle back eventually.",
    Player: "Pure Chance. RÄƒzboi is a game of zero-volition; the deck order is fixed once dealt. However, in physical play, the way you place won cards at the bottom of your deck matters. Grouping face-cards together can lead to 'Streaks' that allow you to win several rounds in a row.\n\nThe 'End-Game' Shuffle: Physical cards often get 'clumped' after a large war. Since wars are often decided by face-cards, if you win a 20-card war, be careful how you order the won cards. Putting your high cards at the very bottom might mean you are vulnerable to a 'War' later when your stack is low.\n\nStamina Management: The game can last a very long time. In competitive settings, 'Card-Tracking' isn't necessary, but mental focus is. If you lose several wars, stay calmâ€”the deck order will cycle back eventually.",
