    intermediate: "The 'End-Game' Shuffle: Physical cards often get 'clumped' after a large war. Since wars are often decided by face-cards, if you win a 20-card war, be careful how you order the won cards. Putting your high cards at the very bottom might mean you are vulnerable to a 'War' later when your stack is low.",
    advanced: "Stamina Management: The game can last a very long time. In competitive settings, 'Card-Tracking' isn't necessary, but mental focus is. If you lose several wars, stay calmâ€”the deck order will cycle back eventually.",
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you are playing with 3+ players, the person with the highest card takes everyone's card. If there's a tie, only the tying players go to war.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "The Ace is the most powerful card; protect it at all costs by hoping it doesn't get drawn into a war against another Ace.",
